@startuml AD_Dashboard_Analytics_Workflow
!theme cerulean-outline
title Dashboard Analytics Workflow (5-Tab Flow)
footer AdventureWorks Sales BI Platform

|#e8f0fe|Admin (Browser)|
|#e8f4e8|React Frontend|
|#fff3e0|ASP.NET Core Backend|
|#fce4ec|Database (AnalyticsDbContext)|

|Admin (Browser)|
start
:Navigate to **/dashboard**\n(Analytics Dashboard);

|React Frontend|
:useEffect triggers\n**loadFilters()** on mount;

#LightBlue:GET /api/dashboard/filters;

|ASP.NET Core Backend|
:DashboardService.GetFiltersAsync();

|Database (AnalyticsDbContext)|
#LightBlue:Query Territories, TerritoryGroups,\nSalesPeople, ShipMethods,\nProductCategories, ProductSubCategories,\nCurrencies;

:Return DashboardFiltersDto;

|React Frontend|
#LightGreen:Populate filter dropdowns:\nDate From/To, Territory,\nTerritory Group, Salesperson,\nShip Method, Category,\nSubcategory, Currency, Online;

:Set initial defaults:\nfrom = "2011-01-01"\nto = "2014-12-30";

:Auto-load **Overview** tab\n(activeTab = 0);

|Admin (Browser)|
:Select filters\n(date range, territory,\ncategory, etc.);

|React Frontend|
#LightYellow:Filter change triggers\nhandleApply() -- clears\nall cached tab data;

:useEffect triggers\nloadActiveTab();

note right
  Each filter change invalidates
  all 5 tab caches, ensuring
  fresh data on next tab visit.
end note

fork
  :=== Tab 0: Overview ===;
  #LightBlue:GET /api/dashboard/overview\nwith DashboardQuery params;
  |ASP.NET Core Backend|
  :DashboardService.GetOverviewAsync();
  :ApplyFilters() builds\nIQueryable<SalesFact>;
  |Database (AnalyticsDbContext)|
  #LightBlue:Execute LINQ queries:\n- Revenue, Orders, Units, AOV\n- On-Time %, Freight %\n- Revenue trend (monthly)\n- Revenue by Category\n- Revenue by Territory\n- Top 10 Products;
  :Return **OverviewDto**\n{ kpis, revenueTrend,\n  revenueByCategory,\n  revenueByTerritory,\n  topProducts };
  |React Frontend|
  #LightGreen:Render **KpiCards**\n(Revenue, Orders, Units,\nAOV, On-Time%, Freight%);
  #LightGreen:Render **ChartCards**:\n- Revenue trend (line)\n- Revenue by territory (bar)\n- Revenue by category (doughnut)\n- Top products (bar);
fork again
  :=== Tab 1: Products ===;
  #LightBlue:GET /api/dashboard/products;
  |ASP.NET Core Backend|
  :DashboardService.GetProductsAsync();
  |Database (AnalyticsDbContext)|
  #LightBlue:Query:\n- Revenue, Units, ASP, Margin %\n- Category/Subcategory matrix\n- Product scatter (Top 10)\n- Discount bands;
  :Return **ProductsDto**;
  |React Frontend|
  #LightGreen:Render KPIs + charts:\n- Category/Subcategory bar\n- Discount bands doughnut\n- Product performance table;
fork again
  :=== Tab 2: Customers ===;
  #LightBlue:GET /api/dashboard/customers;
  |ASP.NET Core Backend|
  :DashboardService.GetCustomersAsync();
  |Database (AnalyticsDbContext)|
  #LightBlue:Query:\n- Active Customers, Rev/Cust\n- Revenue distribution (bins)\n- Top 10 customers\n- Customer trend (monthly);
  :Return **CustomersDto**;
  |React Frontend|
  #LightGreen:Render KPIs + charts:\n- Revenue per customer (bar)\n- Active customers trend (line)\n- Top customers table;
fork again
  :=== Tab 3: Sales Team ===;
  #LightBlue:GET /api/dashboard/salesteam;
  |ASP.NET Core Backend|
  :DashboardService.GetSalesTeamAsync();
  |Database (AnalyticsDbContext)|
  #LightBlue:Query:\n- Revenue, Orders, AOV\n- Leaderboard (Top 20)\n- Quota vs Actual (Top 10)\n- Territory heat map;
  :Return **SalesTeamDto**;
  |React Frontend|
  #LightGreen:Render KPIs + charts:\n- Leaderboard bar\n- Quota vs Actual table;
fork again
  :=== Tab 4: Shipping ===;
  #LightBlue:GET /api/dashboard/shipping;
  |ASP.NET Core Backend|
  :DashboardService.GetShippingAsync();
  |Database (AnalyticsDbContext)|
  #LightBlue:Query:\n- Avg Lead Time, On-Time %,\n  Freight %\n- Lead time by ship method\n- Freight by ship method\n- Lead time by territory;
  :Return **ShippingDto**;
  |React Frontend|
  #LightGreen:Render KPIs + charts:\n- Lead time by method (bar)\n- Freight by method (doughnut)\n- Lead time by territory (bar);
end fork

|Admin (Browser)|
:Switch tabs to view\ndifferent analytics perspectives;

|React Frontend|
#LightYellow:Lazy-load tab data\nonly when tab is first visited\n(and cache is null);

note right
  Tab data is loaded lazily:
  loadActiveTab() checks
  if data is null before
  making an API call.
end note

stop

caption Dashboard — 5-tab analytics powered by DashboardService + AnalyticsDbContext (AdventureWorksDW_Sales)
@enduml
